  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Bertha** (1 review): Bird Song split around Bertha, going Bird Song into Bertha and back into Bird Song, was a highlight [4]\n- **Estimated Prophet** (1 review): Estimated Prophet flowing into Playin' in the Band was a treat; reviewer thinks the Playin' may be the band's best [4]\n- **Diamonds on the Soles of Her Shoes** (1 review): Diamonds on the Soles of Her Shoes and other parts of this show were once on the band's YouTube [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Greatest Story Ever Told**: rare: 12 archived performances [6]\n- **Mexicali Blues**: rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **Diamonds on the Soles of Her Shoes**: rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dac2018-06-09.AKGmix.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 172 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Security debated whether to hassle the tapers, and nearby lawn fans offered support and encouragement [1]\n- A lawn patron shouted at someone and threw belongings over where that person had placed them [1]\n- Mexicali Blues was only the second time played by the band; the first was 2015-11-21 [1]\n- Reviewer attended this and the previous night in Atlanta; Atlanta felt wild, while this night was mellow [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dac2018-06-09.AKGmix.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: DFC lawn, stand at about 8 feet > 2x AKG391 cardioids ORTF and 2x AKG393 hypercardioids pointed at stacks > Zoom F8 @ 44.1kHz/16-bit (4-track) > .wav > SDXC [1]. Also: The original high-quality Nugs version is reportedly no longer findable; only rips from fans' own recordings circulate [5]",
